## Why This Is Asked
Tests a beginner-friendly DP pattern with non-adjacent selections and reconstruction. It also shows handling multiple dimensions (i and t) and a simple heuristic constraint (no two boosts on consecutive days).

## Key Concepts
- DP with two states per index for constrained selections
- Reconstruction of chosen days
- Time/space: O(nk); note can optimize to O(k) space with rolling arrays

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxWorkload(workload, k) {
  const n = workload.length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const noBoost = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const boost = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  noBoost[0][0] = workload[0];
  if (k >= 1) boost[0][1] = 2 * workload[0];
  for (let i = 1; i < n; i++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
      noBoost[i][t] = Math.max(noBoost[i-1][t], boost[i-1][t]) + workload[i];
    }
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      if (noBoost[i-1][t-1] > NEG) boost[i][t] = noBoost[i-1][t-1] + 2*workload[i];
    }
  }
  let best = NEG, bestT = 0, bestS = 0;
  for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
    if (noBoost[n-1][t] > best) { best = noBoost[n-1][t]; bestT = t; bestS = 0; }
    if (boost[n-1][t] > best) { best = boost[n-1][t]; bestT = t; bestS = 1; }
  }
  // reconstruction would backtrack using saved states (omitted for brevity)
  return { maxValue: best, boostedIndices: [] };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This introduces selecting non-covering, fixed-cost segments, a natural DP with a running max optimization. It tests understanding of prefix sums, state pruning, and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Prefix sums to compute segment sums in O(1)
- DP over i and t with exactly t segments
- Running maximum best[t] to avoid O(n) inner loop
- Path reconstruction to recover endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxValueSegments(A, k, c){
  const n = A.length;
  const S = Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++) S[i]=S[i-1]+A[i-1];
  const negInf = -1e18;
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(negInf));
  const par = Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill([-1,-1]));
  dp[0][0]=0;
  for(let t=1;t<=k;t++) par[0][t]=[-1,-1];
  for(let t=1;t<=k;t++){
    let best = negInf; // max of dp[m][t-1]-S[m]
    for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
      best = Math.max(best, dp[i-1][t-1]-S[i-1]);
      const val = best + S[i] - c;
      if(val > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=val; par[i][t]=[i-1,-1]; }
      if(dp[i-1][t] > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=dp[i-1][t]; par[i][t]=[i-1,t]; }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction (simple version)
  let i=n, t=k, ends=[];
  while(t>0){
    const [pi, pt] = par[i][t] || [-1,-1];
    if(pi===-1) break;
    // approximate end at i, start at some m where dp[m][t-1]-S[m] was max
    // for brevity here, return only values; full reconstruction can be added as needed
    ends.push(i);
    i = pi; t--;
  }
  return { value: dp[n][k], ends: ends.reverse() };
}
```

