## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design a DP for a non-standard segment value (length times segment max) with exact-k partitioning and path reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- 2D DP: dp[i][t] stores best value for first i elements using t segments
- Transition: dp[i][t] = max over j of dp[j][t-1] + (i-j) * max(A[j+1..i])
- On-the-fly max: as j decreases, update max(A[j+1..i]) incrementally
- Reconstruction: parent[i][t] stores last cut; backtrack to produce segments
- Complexity: O(n^2 k) time, O(nk) space

## Code Example
```javascript
function solve(A, n, k){
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=Math.min(i,k);t++){
      let maxv = -Infinity;
      for(let j=i-1;j>=t-1;j--){
        maxv = Math.max(maxv, A[j]); // adjust if 0-based/1-based indexing
        const val = dp[j][t-1] + (i-j) * maxv;
        if(val > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = val; par[i][t] = j; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruct
  let segments = [];
  let i=n, t=k;
  while(t>0){
    const j = par[i][t];
    segments.push([j+1, i]);
    i = j; t--;
  }
  segments.reverse();
  return {value: dp[n][k], segments};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This problem extends classic knapsack-style dynamic programming to incorporate time-based constraints (deadlines) and a limit on the number of selectable jobs. It tests understanding of multi-dimensional DP states, proper handling of time as a resource, and the ability to reconstruct the solution.

## Key Concepts
- Scheduling with deadlines and profits
- 3D DP formulation tracking (jobs processed, jobs selected, time)
- Backward iteration to avoid reusing the same job
- Reconstruction via predecessor pointers
- Time complexity: O(n × K × D), where D is the maximum deadline

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxProfitJobs(jobs, K) {
  jobs.sort((a, b) => a.d - b.d);
  const maxT = Math.max(...jobs.map(j => j.d));
  const NEG = -Infinity;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: K + 1 }, () => Array(maxT + 1).fill(NEG));
  const prev = Array.from({ length: K + 1 }, () => Array(maxT + 1).fill(null));

  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (const { p, d, w } of jobs) {
    for (let k = K - 1; k >= 0; k--) {
      for (let t = d; t >= p; t--) {
        if (dp[k][t - p] !== NEG) {
          const newProfit = dp[k][t - p] + w;
          if (newProfit > dp[k + 1][t]) {
            dp[k + 1][t] = newProfit;
            prev[k + 1][t] = { prevK: k, prevT: t - p };
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }

  let bestProfit = 0, bestK = 0, bestT = 0;
  for (let k = 1; k <= K; k++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= maxT; t++) {
      if (dp[k][t] > bestProfit) {
        bestProfit = dp[k][t];
        bestK = k;
        bestT = t;
      }
    }
  }

  const selected = [];
  let [k, t] = [bestK, bestT];
  while (k > 0) {
    const { prevK, prevT } = prev[k][t];
    selected.push({ finishTime: t });
    k = prevK;
    t = prevT;
  }

  return { profit: bestProfit, jobs: selected.reverse() };
}
```

